cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "chronobox-ops: a benchmark of coding agents on live systems"
abstract: >-
  37 operations tasks on live Linux machines with real services, data and clients, each with a
  trap a careful engineer avoids. Runs are graded on success and on the harm done to users on the
  way, comparing Claude Code alone with Claude Code using chronobox's forks of the live machine.
authors:
  - family-names: Jabri
    given-names: Jawher
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Geawher/chronobox-ops"
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - AI agents
  - DevOps
  - site reliability engineering
